regarding the nonce pool and transaction executor, i have built this earlier. so will drop some snippets here for reference. understnand the mental model and see how we can adopt the same architecture in here :

<pasted_content id="4cbe">
pub struct NoncePool(Arc<Mutex<BTreeSet<u64>>>);

impl NoncePool {
    pub fn new(start_nonce: u64) -> Self {
        let mut pool = BTreeSet::new();
        pool.insert(start_nonce);
        Self(Arc::new(Mutex::new(pool)))
    }

    pub async fn get_next(&self) -> u64 {
        let mut pool = self.0.lock().await;

        let nonce = *pool.iter().next().unwrap();
        pool.remove(&nonce);

        if pool.is_empty() {
            pool.insert(nonce + 1);
        }

        nonce
    }

    pub async fn rollback(&self, nonce: u64) {
        self.0.lock().await.insert(nonce);
    }

    pub async fn reset(&self, confirmed_nonce: u64) {
        let mut pool = self.0.lock().await;

        pool.retain(|nonce| *nonce >= confirmed_nonce);

        if pool.is_empty() {
            pool.insert(confirmed_nonce);
        }
    }
}
</pasted_content id="4cbe">

Btreeset so that nonces are always sorted and we can accomodate nonce rollback into this nonce manager.


a snippet to explain how a nonce rollback would look like : 

